    "key": "services",
    "templateKey": "repobot-services",
    "title": "Contractor & remodeling",
    "description": "A local service business site: services with honest starting prices, a draggable before/after project gallery, a live open/closed badge with click-to-call, testimonials, credentials, and a quote-request form — a multi-page site edited in one content file.",
    "marketingExampleTitle": "Local service business",
    "category": "services",
    "homePath": "/",
    "previewPath": "/services",
    "homeViewDir": "web/app/src/View/Services",
    "base": "landing",
    "clientOnly": true,
    "capabilities": ["IOS", "ANDROID"],
    "isDefault": false,
    "forms": {
        "$comment": "Managed-form kinds, formKey -> kind (append-only vocabulary: RSVP | LEAD | MAILING_LIST | PROOFING). Compose stamps these into repobot.deploy.json as formKinds; the dashboard renders declared kinds as typed views and keeps the raw Inbox for undeclared keys.",
        "quote-request": "LEAD"
    },
    "theme": {
        "$comment": "The sitework register's brand overlay: the preset's safety-orange accent as the project brand, so app-side surfaces wear the same trades register as the marketing pages instead of the kernel default blue. Values match the sitework preset's own light/dark accents — the marketing pages resolve brand over preset accent, so keeping them identical means the overlay re-brands the app without shifting the pages.",
        "brand": {
            "primary": "#c2410c",
            "primaryDark": "#ff8a3d"
        }
    },
    "contentContract": {
        "$comment": "The pack's content slots, as data (packs/README.md 'Content contract'). Declares what a composer (agent or tool) must bind for a generated variant of this pack to present as real: slot paths into the typed content module, their kinds, and minimums. The demo business is a remodeling contractor, but the slots are trade-agnostic — a plumber, landscaper, or cleaner variant binds the same shape. The ticker, build-log, materials, and color-deck slots are optional (no minimum): the pages drop a section whose list is empty. Authored alongside the module and guarded by the pack's content tests — the module satisfies the contract; the contract never drifts ahead of it.",
        "module": "web/app/src/View/Services/content.ts",
